{
  "title": "Namaz for Fulfillment of Needs (3)",
  "data": "After the taslim and the glorification (tasbih), recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) fifty-one times, and then say each of the following fifty times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHA\nI seek forgiveness of Allah.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.\nلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nLAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL A’ZEEM\nThere is no might and no strength save in Allah, the High, the Great.\nThen say the following supplication:\nيَا اَللّٰهُ الْمَانِعُ قُدْرَتَهٗ خَلْقَهٗ\nYAA ALLAAHUL MAANE-O’ QUDRATAHU KHALQAHU\nO Allah, Who withholds His power from His creatures,\nوَالْمَالِكُ بِهَا سُلْطَانَهٗ\nWAL MAALEKO BEHAA SULTAANAHU\nand through it holds His dominion,\nوَالْمُتَسَلِّطُ بِمَا فِيْ يَدَيْهِ عَلٰى كُلِّ مَوْجُوْدٍ\nWAL MOTASALLETO BEMAA FEE YADAYHE A’LAA KULLE MAWJOODIN\nand by what is in His hands has authority over everything that exists!\nوَغَيْرُكَ يَخِيْبُ رَجَآءُ رَاجِيْهِ\nWA GHAYROKA YAKHEEBO RAJAAA-O RAAJEEHE\nWhoever hopes in other than You is disappointed in his hope,\nوَرَاجِيْكَ مَسْرُوْرٌ لَا يَخِيْبُ\nWA RAAJEEKA MASROORUN LAA YAKHEEBO\nbut whoever hopes in You is gladdened and never disappointed.\nاَسْئَلُكَ بِكُلِّ رِضًى لَكَ\nAS-ALOKA BEKULLE REZAN LAKA\nI ask You by everything that pleases You,\nوَبِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ اَنْتَ فِيْهِ\nWA BEKULLE SHAY-IN ANTA FEEHE\nby everything in which You are,\nوَبِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ تُحِبُّ اَنْ تُذْكَرَ بِهٖ\nWA BEKULLE SHAY-IN TOHIBBO AN TUZKARA BEHI\nby everything by which You love to be remembered,\nوَبِكَ يَا اَللّٰهُ فَلَيْسَ يَعْدِلُكَ شَيْءٌ\nWA BEKA YAA ALLAAHO FALAYSA YA’DELOKA SHAY-UN\nand by You, O Allah, for nothing is equal to You,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TOSALLEYA A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nto send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَتَحْفَظَنِيْ وَوَلَدِيْ وَاَهْلِيْ وَمَالِيْ\nWA TAHFAZANEE WA WALADEE WA AHLEE WA MAALEE\nto safeguard me, my children, my family and my property,\nوَتَحْفَظَنِيْ بِحِفْظِكَ\nWA TAHFAZANEE BEHIFZEKA\nto guard me with Your guarding,\nوَاَنْ تَقْضِيَ حَاجَتِيْ فِيْ كَذَا وَكَذَا\nWA AN TAQZEYA HAAJATEE FEE KAZAA WA KAZAA\nand to settle my need concerning such-and-such.\nMention your need in place of \"such-and-such\".",
  "merits": "Sayyid Ibn Tawus, in his book of al-Mazar (chapter: Rites of al-Kufah Mosque), after mentioning the recommended acts at Imam Ali (a.s.)'s niche (mihrab), has mentioned a special prayer for settling the needs to be offered there.\nIt consists of four units, each two alone (the taslim is said after every two units). In the first unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) ten times; in the second, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) twenty-one times; in the third, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) thirty-one times; and in the fourth, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) forty-one times."
}
